  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness by comparing the probability of unfavorable outcomes to favorable ones and preferring the more right-skewed lottery. In this case, Lottery B has a 20% chance of 0€ (unfavorable) and an 80% chance of 4000€ (favorable), meaning it is left-skewed, not right-skewed. Therefore, no lottery is right-skewed, so the reason is not applicable. The individual’s report does not mention skewness, nor does it consider the relative probability of unfavorable versus favorable outcomes. Instead, the individual focuses on the higher potential gain and the high probability of winning, which reflects an expected value-based or risk-averse reasoning, not skewness-based reasoning. Since the relevant information for the reason is absent and the justification does not reflect the rule of the reason, the individual did not use the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
